{% comment %}
  Reusable FTC-compliant affiliate-disclosure box.

  Where this goes in Shopify:
    Online Store → Themes → ... → Edit code → Snippets → Add a new
    snippet → name it "affiliate-disclosure" → paste this file.

  How to use it:
    Insert this line at the very top of every buying-guide article
    body (above the first product mention), and at the top of every
    /products/ template that promotes affiliate purchases:

      {% render 'affiliate-disclosure' %}

    For the Shopify blog editor (rich text), wrap the snippet in a
    Liquid include via a custom blog template, or paste the rendered
    HTML directly into the article body. See pages/affiliate-disclosure.md
    for the full standalone page.

  Why:
    FTC 16 CFR Part 255 requires that material connections (paid
    commissions for product recommendations) be disclosed clearly
    and conspicuously, near the relevant claim, before the consumer
    sees the link. A footer-only disclosure is not compliant.
{% endcomment %}
<aside class="affiliate-disclosure"
       role="note"
       aria-label="Affiliate disclosure"
       style="border:1px solid #d0d7de;background:#f6f8fa;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 24px;border-radius:6px;font-size:0.95em;line-height:1.45;">
  <strong>Affiliate disclosure:</strong>
  WC Safety is reader-supported. When you buy through links on this
  page we may earn a commission from the retailer, at no extra cost
  to you. We only recommend products we believe meet the safety
  standards described in our
  <a href="/pages/editorial-methodology">editorial methodology</a>.
  See our full
  <a href="/pages/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>
  for details.
</aside>
